	<Description>A high-frequency source irradiates a diffractive lattice. The lattice diffracts the radiation preferentially in specific directions, similar to a crystal structure in an X-ray beam. By rotating the "crystal" lattice, the diffraction angles change. By measuring the angles of the diffracted beams, the lattice structure can in principle be solved.</Description>
